# Identity strings for this device, read by systemd (hostnamectl, and the About
# panel of the session's settings).
#
# PRETTY_HOSTNAME rather than /etc/hostname: a static hostname cannot contain a
# space, so "Rongyue E5" lives here and the login prompt keeps using the static
# name (e5-linux).
#
# HARDWARE_VENDOR/HARDWARE_MODEL are deliberately not set.  They fill the
# "Hardware Model" row, and the part name belongs in the "Processor" row -- which
# nothing in userspace can write: it is built from /proc/cpuinfo, so it is fixed
# in the kernel instead (kernel/patches/0009, docs/FINDINGS.md section 22).
PRETTY_HOSTNAME=Rongyue E5
